lue" "Let's introduce the new variable $u={x}^{2}+1.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {6}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {6}^{u}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-73801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C"] ["math" "{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}+C"] ["math" "{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{6}^{{x}^{2}+1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int 4x\\,{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=4{x}^{2}-3.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x\\,{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int {4}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{u}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-73665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\cdot {4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}+C"] ["math" "{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{4}^{4{x}^{2}-3}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int x{8}^{3{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=3{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{8}^{3{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {8}^{3{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {8}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int {8}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\frac{{8}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{8}^{3{x}^{2}}}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-31420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x{8}^{3{x}^{2}}}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{8}^{3x}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{8}^{3{x}^{2}}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{8}^{3{x}^{2}}}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{8}^{3{x}^{2}}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{8}^{3{x}^{2}}}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-211989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int {x}^{2}{4}^{{x}^{3}/5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-211989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{5}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{4}^{{x}^{3}/5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {4}^{{x}^{3}/5}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {4}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\int {4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot {4}^{u}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{3}/5}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-211989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-211989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-211989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{3}/5}}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{3}/5}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{3}}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{{x}^{3}/5}}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{4}^{{x}^{3}}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-211989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{3}/5}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{{5}^{x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u={5}^{x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,\\text{d}u={5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{{5}^{x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{5}^{x}+1}\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{5}^{x}+1|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that ${5}^{x}+1>0$ for all $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-31478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-113852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int 2{e}^{3x}{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-113852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{3x}+2.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u=2{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{e}^{3x}{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}\\cdot 2{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-113852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-113852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-113852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{3}}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{6}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-113852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+2)}^{4}}{6}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{{4}^{x}}{{4}^{x}+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u={4}^{x}+2.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}u={4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{4}^{x}}{{4}^{x}+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{4}^{x}+2}\\cdot {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{4}^{x}+2|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that ${4}^{x}+2>0$ for all $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-31480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-31480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x}+2)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int {2}^{x+1}\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u={2}^{x}-5.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & ={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}u={2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {2}^{x+1}\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\cdot {2}^{x}\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{(\\frac{3}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {u}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-73669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{{2}^{x}-5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-73669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{({2}^{x}-5)^{3}}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-49577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\int 5{e}^{x}\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-49577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{x}+4.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u={e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{e}^{x}\\sqrt{{e}^{x}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\sqrt{{e}^{x}+4}\\cdot {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-49577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-49577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-49577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\sqrt[3]{({e}^{x}+4)^{2}}+C"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{5}}+C"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{3}\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-49577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10}{3}\\sqrt{({e}^{x}+4)^{3}}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {3}^{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=2x+1.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {3}^{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{3}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\,|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}({3}^{3}-{3}^{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(27-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-350743" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350743" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{24}{\\ln(3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\frac{12{e}^{x}}{3{e}^{x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=3{e}^{x}+1.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $7$ | $16$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\frac{12{e}^{x}}{3{e}^{x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\frac{4}{3{e}^{x}+1}\\cdot 3{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{7}^{16}\\frac{4}{u}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{7}^{16}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{7}^{16} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{16}{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-350751" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-350751" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\ln(\\frac{16}{7})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-346400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\cdot {3}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-346400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\cdot {3}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\,|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}({3}^{1}-{3}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(3-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-346400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-346400" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-346400" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{\\ln(3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}}\\frac{1}{5}x{e}^{2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}}\\frac{1}{5}x{e}^{2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}}{e}^{2{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}({e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(25-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-30953" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30953" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30953" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}x{4}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{4}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{4}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{4}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{{4}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c03415efc1a91baf90ef6ea0bb44e8676f8d098a08fbb4519f1076eb900f372d"} {"question" "q-30978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "q-30978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/state.json" "file_sha256" "5a46d6dffd12e126b6cbbbfc5cbffd581d8051987cd494674ed63b44ae7ebbe5"} {"question" "e-14402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate  $\\displaystyle{\\int x^2 e^{x^3+1}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14402.json" "file_sha256" "db0952effad7c286d51051182c6f5ecdaa04afbae77f4396ca12fd033facf2c8"} {"question" "e-14402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u = x^3+1.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm{d}u = x^2 \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{{x}^{3}+1}\\cdot \\,{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{{x}^{3}+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14402.json" "file_sha256" "db0952effad7c286d51051182c6f5ecdaa04afbae77f4396ca12fd033facf2c8"} {"question" "e-14403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate  $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14403.json" "file_sha256" "9a7749f936e42dd3af34b6343aba853d7956952f11a5abc08656827028fae64c"} {"question" "e-14403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u= 1-x^4.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\textrm{d}u}{ \\textrm{d}x} = -4x^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x = -\\dfrac{1}{4} \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\int {x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} }\\, \\textrm{d}x \n&=\\int {{3^{1-x^4}}\\cdot x^3 }\\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n&=  \\int {3^{u}} \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right) \\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n                                                     &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\int {3^{u}}  \\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n                                                     &=  -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\dfrac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C\\[5pt]\n                                                     &=   -\\dfrac{3^{1-x^4}}{4\\ln 3}+ C.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14403.json" "file_sha256" "9a7749f936e42dd3af34b6343aba853d7956952f11a5abc08656827028fae64c"} {"question" "e-14404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate  $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {e^{2x}} {e^{2x} + 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14404.json" "file_sha256" "437b89b1bcbc196a04509f95038f5636b29292fffc32347615b5f5ff4b792ba1"} {"question" "e-14404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u = e^{2x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 2e^{2x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\, \\textrm{d}u = e^{2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x}}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}+1|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}+1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that $e^{2x} + 1 > 0$ for all $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14404.json" "file_sha256" "437b89b1bcbc196a04509f95038f5636b29292fffc32347615b5f5ff4b792ba1"} {"question" "e-14407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt {\\ln 4}} 16xe^{-2x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14407.json" "file_sha256" "ba6830c3489bf593519e7a7b63fde36873baa022b41e8a8b41a35f5fdb972c5f"} {"question" "e-14407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's introduce the new variable $u=-2x^2.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-4x\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n-4 \\, \\textrm{d}u=16x \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt {\\ln 4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2\\ln 4$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}16x{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot 16x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{u}\\cdot (-4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-4({e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{16}-1) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{15}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14407.json" "file_sha256" "ba6830c3489bf593519e7a7b63fde36873baa022b41e8a8b41a35f5fdb972c5f"}] "usage" {"q-113852" [] "e-14407" [] "q-31420" [] "e-14402" [] "e-14403" [] "e-14404" []} "basis" 1138 "retractions" [[17592186184688 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\intx8^{3x^{2}}dx$."] [17592186184394 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int2e^{3x}(e^{3x} + 2)^{3}dx$."] [17592186183892 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int x^2 e^{x^3+1}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186183892 :question/worked-solution "Let's introduce the new variable\n\n$$\nu = x^3+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm{d}u = x^2 \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}e^{x^{3} + 1}dx &= \\inte^{x^{3} + 1} \\cdot x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\inte^{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\inte^{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}e^{u} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}e^{x^{3} + 1} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186183893 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186183893 :question/worked-solution "Let's introduce the new variable $u= 1-x^4$. Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = -4x^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x = -\\dfrac{1}{4} \\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int {x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}}}\\, \\textrm{d}x &=\\int {{3^{1-x^4}}\\cdot x^3}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &= \\int {3^{u}} \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right) \\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\int {3^{u}} \\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\dfrac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{3^{1-x^4}}{4\\ln 3}+ C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186183894 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {e^{2x}} {e^{2x} + 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186183894 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable\n\n$$\nu = e^{2x}+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 2e^{2x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\, \\textrm{d}u = e^{2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{e^{2x}}{e^{2x} + 1}dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{e^{2x} + 1} \\cdot e^{2x}dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\frac{1}{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln & e^{2x} + 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (e^{2x} + 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that $e^{2x} + 1 > 0$ for all $x$."] [17592186183895 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt {\\ln 4}} 16xe^{-2x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186183895 :question/worked-solution "Let's introduce the new variable $u=-2x^2$. Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-4x \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad -4 \\, \\textrm{d}u=16x \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt {\\ln 4}$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2\\ln 4$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\ln 4}}16xe^{-2x^{2}}dx &= \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\ln 4}}e^{-2x^{2}} \\cdot 16xdx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{-2\\ln 4}e^{u} \\cdot (-4du) \\\\\n&=-4\\int_{0}^{-2\\ln 4}e^{u}du \\\\\n&= \\left.- 4e^{u}\\right|_{0}^{-2\\ln 4} \\\\\n&=-4(e^{-2\\ln 4} - e^{0}) \\\\\n&=-4(\\frac{1}{16} - 1) \\\\\n&= 4(\\frac{15}{16}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{15}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186180814 17592186180815 17592186180816 17592186180817 17592186180818 17592186183018 17592186183019 17592186183020 17592186183021 17592186183022] "immutable_fields" [[17592186180813 :answer-field/correct] [17592186180813 :answer-field/id] [17592186180813 :answer-field/key] [17592186180813 :answer-field/type] [17592186183017 :answer-field/correct] [17592186183017 :answer-field/id] [17592186183017 :answer-field/key] [17592186183017 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
